e G.Doubleday C.Manning G.Piddington A.E.Taylor L.Bishop N.Dewberry C.MacLe[illegible]an Mrs.","A witty speech by our President (\"the jumpers are jumping higher, the throwers throwing further, the walkers walking faster - and we're expecting the runners any minute now\" - howls of derision from G.","G.Biscoe","G.Biscoe","W.Kerr 12:23 (16); H.Evans 12:35 (14); S.Masterson 12:48 (13); T.Hart 12:36 (11); B.Taylor 13:35 (13); G.Biscoe 14:27 (14).","79. · G.Biscoe · 5:33","G.Biscoe","BISCOE G.","G.","Again at the end of the financial year I thank all the following members for donations. G.Biscoe, C.Brooks, J.V.Baker, C.T.Carter, R.J.Carter, D.Crookes, L. Coleman, N.Dewberry, G.Doubleday, P.Duncan, E.Donovan, Mrs.","86. · G.Biscoe · 5:56","46. · G. Biscoe · 5:55","3. · L.Lyons · 4.46 · D.McMillan · 5.12 · G.Biscoe · 5.59 · J.Neillis · 5.30","G.Biscoe · 6.20","We were 9th in the Senior, 16th in the Junior with G Biscoe in the team, and 8th in the Youths with George Flanagan in the scoring four. On the track the Leyton Floodlit Meeting on a cold blustery evening saw Dennis Merrett, Ted Gaworski, John Bromley and Bob Taylor among a good Club turn out."]}